{"c":[{"id":"7fe6bd97a37920c6","sum":"Helper: leak-check one string per line; mv scripts, never edit a running one; never mutate w.nodes; request walks need frontmostPid; expiry only in lifetimes.ts. Host: machines decide, coordinators draw (Rig+ManualClock); renders need SwiftUI controls; tests own --settings.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"901960440bd057da","sum":"Helper traps B6-B9: leak-check is quadratic per line; mv a new bash script over a running one; never mutate w.nodes; pair focused:true with frontmostPid; fake-app pauses on a click; offer expiry only in lifetimes.ts; judge perf on real probes.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"fd5a5290914f4366","sum":"Helper traps: leak-check.ts is quadratic per line (check one string per line); never edit a running bash script, mv a new one over it; never mutate w.nodes (WeakMap caches per state); focused:true from a request walk needs model.frontmostPid too.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d6128635107f5dca","sum":"Long-input traps: leak-check.ts hashes every word-bounded substring per line (quadratic; 50 KB NDJSON lines never finish, check one string per line); never edit a running bash script in place, write a new file and mv it over (B6).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T201045Z-36d6a210e08a778d","text":"leak-check.ts hashes every word-bounded substring of each line (quadratic in line length): an NDJSON with 50 KB lines never finishes; check one string per line instead.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T201045Z-88beaae782960744","text":"Never edit a running bash script in place (bash reads it as it runs); write a new file and mv it over, as B6 did with run-audit.sh mid-audit.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"894a99a3e4795948","sum":"Screen model: apply builds a new WindowState and nodes Map per snapshot (candidates.ts/descriptor.ts cache per state in WeakMaps), so never mutate w.nodes; a request walk says focused:true for a background app's window, so pair model.focusedWindowId with frontmostPid.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T201045Z-f95178d8fbcf4b52","text":"ScreenModel.apply builds a new WindowState and nodes Map per snapshot; candidates.ts and descriptor.ts cache per-state indexes in WeakMaps, so never mutate w.nodes in place.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T223858Z-64661b6aeffb7a85","text":"caret-screen's request walk (AppWorker walkWindow .request) reports focused:true for a background app's own focused window, so the helper's model.focusedWindowId alone does not mean the user is there; check model.frontmostPid (from appSwitch and frontmost focus events) too.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"d3f84837adf559a9","sum":"Helper lore B8-B9: fake-app executor pauses on a click, not a key; offer expiry only in offers/lifetimes.ts; judge generator perf on real audit probes, not synthetic scenes; hand entry into a loopFinish settles first, partial matches re-offer the rest.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"364dcf1bfeba4910","sum":"Fake-app executor window is unfocused: tests pause it with a click in its frame, not a key; offer expiry lives only in offers/lifetimes.ts and records stay until offerWithdrawn (B8).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T231108Z-16725ff4ed3b6a48","text":"test/fake-app.ts's executor window is not focused, so a key userInput pauses nothing there; tests use a click inside its frame instead.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T231108Z-7306e773123a8d65","text":"Offer expiry lives only in helper/src/offers/lifetimes.ts: the host-offer registry keeps a record until its offerWithdrawn, and a loop going idle no longer withdraws its offers (B8).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4f388ef10e3dd3cf","sum":"Judge generator perf on real-window audit probes, not synthetic scenes (a 10x synthetic win slowed real cold calls, reverted, B8); hand entry into a loopFinish is judged after EDIT_SETTLE_MS: partial re-offers the rest under a new key, mismatch is stale (B9).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T021618Z-ea65f8fc10f79055","text":"Generator perf: judge changes by real-window audit probes (run-audit.sh PROBE_SECONDS, event-loop CPU via process.threadCpuUsage), not synthetic scenes; a row-sorted label index won 10x synthetically but slowed real cold calls (p95 5.3->7.4 ms) and was reverted (B8).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T032052Z-1661c0e7f0a95c07","text":"Hand entry into a loopFinish/routine is judged after EDIT_SETTLE_MS of stillness (typing passes through prefixes): partial matches re-offer the rest under a new key (offerWithdrawn reoffered + replacedBy); a mismatch is stale; all entered is taken at once (B9).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"778dd63682e2697d","sum":"apps/caret: SurfaceMachine/FillMachine decide, coordinators read and draw; test via SurfaceRig/FillRig + ManualClock. Off-screen renders: SwiftUI-drawn controls only; no repeating KeyframeAnimator (CPU). Debug JSON omits nil. Host tests: own --settings, --status-item off.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"f9666f0bda0d6429","sum":"Host: repeating KeyframeAnimator redraws off screen (10.9% CPU; use Timer blinks); debug JSON omits nil, test == null. XCTestCase.record(_:) shadows a free record(...): name it taskRecord. Perch checks run headless: real Helper, fake-app.ts reader, --perch hidden, pid 5150.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"40c277ae98ccebf5","sum":"A repeating SwiftUI KeyframeAnimator redraws every frame even off screen (perch blink+breath cost 10.9% of a core; one-shot Timer blinks ~1%). The host's debug-socket JSON omits nil optionals, so scripts test == null, not === null.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T213409Z-2c06a8e735f40a5c","text":"A repeating SwiftUI KeyframeAnimator redraws every frame, even through long holds and in a panel never ordered on screen: the perch's 5 s blink plus breath cost the host 10.9% of a core; one-shot blinks on a Timer cost about 1%.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T213409Z-cab3b62b740f0600","text":"The host's debug-socket JSON omits nil optionals (Swift JSONEncoder), so scripts must test == null / undefined, not === null.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b1c45b8f5a3c01de","sum":"Tests: in XCTestCase subclasses a free function record(...) is shadowed by XCTestCase.record(_:), so name builders taskRecord. Perch/taskControl checks run with nothing on screen: real Helper with helper/test/fake-app.ts as readerLink, host --perch hidden --allow-pids 5150.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261002T213409Z-d226423d62147f07","text":"In XCTestCase subclasses a free function named record(...) is shadowed by XCTestCase.record(_:); name test builders taskRecord or similar.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T213410Z-c55d0036facdd019","text":"Perch and taskControl checks can run with nothing on screen: real Helper in process with helper/test/fake-app.ts as readerLink, host with --perch hidden and --allow-pids 5150 (no such process).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"aa279d8cb1624e15","sum":"apps/caret: SurfaceMachine/FillMachine decide, coordinators only read and draw; test with SurfaceRig/FillRig and a ManualClock. ImageRenderer draws AppKit controls as placeholders: render SwiftUI-drawn ones. Host tests: own --settings, --status-item off.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"97ae8d03f0e99759","sum":"x","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T020832Z-18f641c9e903d593","text":"apps/caret: surface decisions (hold, retry, withdraw, work line, toast undo, Esc/Cmd-Z) live in CaretHostCore SurfaceMachine; SurfaceCoordinator only reads AppKit and draws. Test a surface change with SurfaceRig steps and a ManualClock, not on screen.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T022431Z-7481bd50921d0954","text":"apps/caret: fill decisions (proposal hold, withdraw, toast lifetime, its Cmd-Z grant) live in CaretHostCore FillMachine; FillCoordinator only reads AX and draws. Test with FillRig; the shared toast slot with SharedToastSlotTests.TwoOwners (one arbiter).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"fea98e93de0597e3","sum":"ImageRenderer draws AppKit controls (Button, Toggle, ProgressView) as placeholders: off-screen renders need SwiftUI-drawn controls, as OnboardingView does. Host test runs: pass --settings <own file> and --status-item off; --onboarding defaults off.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T024925Z-053830fa0ce54d2d","text":"SwiftUI ImageRenderer draws AppKit-backed controls (stock Button, Toggle, ProgressView) as placeholders; off-screen renders of a window need every control drawn in SwiftUI with custom styles, as Onboarding/OnboardingView does.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T024925Z-d69b7ed0397e33f9","text":"Caret host test runs: pass --settings <own file> and --status-item off; --onboarding defaults to off so a launch never puts a window up (auto opens it until finished once).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0dd92c41dd581009","sum":"B9-B14: fixture 'activate legacy'/'quit PID' moves the front; Jev requests go through SnippetLedger (all windows, chats <=600 chars); routine proof 3 hits Balanced/2 Eager; fill kinds whole or not at all; host needs caretRectAX; popup acceptance needs --act-pids.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"04d29e5067469439","sum":"B9/B10: fixture --foreground takes the front on 'activate legacy', 'quit PID' returns it; Jev requests go through a SnippetLedger; routine proof 3 hits Balanced, 2 Eager. B11 chat cap 600 chars. Host needs caretRectAX; fill_acceptance popup needs --act-pids.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ef7f0d6980690f67","sum":"B9/B10: fixture --foreground takes the front on 'activate legacy', 'quit PID' returns it; every Jev request takes screen text through a SnippetLedger (privacy.test checks); routine proof is 3 silent hits at Balanced, 2 at Eager, off at Quiet.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2c2a04358afd7dde","sum":"Fixture --foreground takes the front in ~100 ms on 'activate legacy' and 'quit PID' returns it in ~250 ms (B9). Every Jev request takes screen text through a SnippetLedger and sets req.snippets; privacy.test fails on undeclared lines or over-budget windows (B10).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T032315Z-0691c078778b7697","text":"CaretFixture.app --foreground becomes frontmost in ~100 ms on stdin 'activate legacy' (NSApp.activate(ignoringOtherApps:)); macOS 14 NSApp.activate() never did from the background; 'quit PID' hands the foreground back within ~250 ms (B9, run-activation-proof.sh).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T043507Z-396591a0dafeb49c","text":"Every Jev request builder must take its screen text through a SnippetLedger (helper/src/privacy.ts) and set req.snippets; test/privacy.test.ts fails on any undeclared window line, over 1,200 chars from one window, or half of a non-card window (B10).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f287a62811635a9e","sum":"Routine proof follows the level (Balanced 3 silent hits, Eager 2, off at Quiet; offers/settings.ts LEVELS); tests and evals built on two hits pass settings level eager (B10).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T043510Z-072d273b831b9d6f","text":"x","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T043537Z-5d59f5b5da2447c5","text":"Routine proof follows the level (Balanced 3 silent hits, Eager 2, off at Quiet; helper/src/offers/settings.ts LEVELS); tests and evals built on two hits pass settings level eager (B10).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"71aa6c674c93d84d","sum":"B11 conversations give under half their text, at most 600 chars per Jev request; the cap can cause wrong fills (cut meeting block). Host surfaces need caretRectAX, not AppKit caretRect. fill_acceptance popup needs reader --act-pids.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"89eb27a1038b36eb","sum":"B11: conversations (conversation.ts) give under half their text and at most 600 chars per Jev request; the cap can cause wrong fills, not just blanks (cut meeting block, Meeting date got the order's Placed date in live-replay.ts).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T051909Z-10a9c6959d310436","text":"The conversation cap can cause wrong fills, not just blanks: with calibration sources relabelled as Messages it cut the meeting block and Jev filled Meeting date with the order's Placed date (scripts/live-replay.ts, B11).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T051909Z-f82b591e5e9c3894","text":"Conversations (helper/src/conversation.ts: chat/mail bundle, composer under 3+ message lines, or stamped sender rows) give under half their text and at most 600 chars per Jev request, however short; the ledger also charges lines a taken text contains (B11).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"f2649e800ab24c86","sum":"Host gate, surfaces and perch need FocusedFieldSnapshot.caretRectAX (caretRect is AppKit bottom-left). fill_acceptance popup needs the reader with --act-pids, or the executor stops notAllowed ('The form changed').","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T054535Z-cd383e079c08d5e3","text":"Host: KeyType's FocusedFieldSnapshot.caretRect is AppKit (bottom-left); the gate, surfaces and perch need FocusedFieldSnapshot.caretRectAX, or the gate tests a mirrored point and holds ghost text as covered.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T054535Z-f725bb7f07997327","text":"fill_acceptance popup needs the reader started with --act-pids: the executor writes through reader verbs, and without it the run stops with notAllowed and the host shows 'The form changed'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6d79d123a20fb2f7","sum":"B12-B14 fill: kinds whole or not at all; SnippetLedger over all model windows; kindless and name fields withheld only on cuts that touch them. Tests: replay deltas <3/78 are noise; bind harness to the beforeEach server; fix the generator clock.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6786333f0fb04e09","sum":"B12-B13 fill privacy: kinds go whole or not at all; SnippetLedger over model.windows.values() charges every window showing a text; keep close-on-miss outside kind groups; a kindless field is withheld only for cuts touching its label words or a typed value.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"5f02cf50c6404d08","sum":"B12: conversation fill offers each kind a field takes whole or not at all (bare values let Jev pick a padding link); SnippetLedger charges per window, so packing short spans after a miss overran a chat budget; keep close-on-miss outside kind groups.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T060232Z-ab20cd82e4a1331c","text":"Fill from a conversation offers each kind a field takes whole (every typed value, each with label/section/block) or not at all; letting values in bare to fit the ~220-char chat budget made Jev pick a padding thread's link at 0.76 (B12 live-run5, candidates.ts byRelevance).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T060243Z-76a84ab97345f4dc","text":"privacy.test counts a window line shown by any window's text in a request; SnippetLedger charges per window, so packing short spans after a miss pushed a 192-char chat to 104 covered on a 95 budget (B12). Keep close-on-miss outside kind groups.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"15d4fcad6f30cb62","sum":"B13: build SnippetLedger over model.windows.values() (it charges every window showing a text, refuses if any is over). A kindless fill field is withheld only when a cut took a typed value or left out a line sharing its label words.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T075125Z-769f076b2b26d50b","text":"SnippetLedger(windows) charges a taken text to every window that shows it, either way round (line inside the text, or text inside a line); refuses when any of them is over budget. Build it over model.windows.values(), never just the source window (B13).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T075154Z-10f895f4b8d309e7","text":"A fill field whose label names no kind is withheld when a cut took a typed value or a cut conversation left out a line sharing its label words; withholding it on any cut blanked Name on the fill desk (unrelated team chat always cut) and lost the first-look offer (B13 live-final).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6e542726e07d67d3","sum":"B13-B14 testing: replay deltas under ~3/78 are Jev noise; socket harnesses bind to the beforeEach's HelperServer; fix the generator clock for load-proof tests. Names are a fill kind withheld only when namesCut.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"be073912f9f26071","sum":"Live replay deltas under ~3 of 78 fields are Jev noise; rerun with --variants/--rules/--fixes (B13). Socket test harnesses bind publish/sendToReader to the HelperServer made in that beforeEach, or a late 'stopped' leaks into the next test (B14).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T075211Z-5ac7a437648ff4d5","text":"Live replay noise: the same code gave 24, 26, 27 and 25 of 78 on 'sources in Messages' rule on (B13); pre-ask withholding is deterministic, so differences under about 3 fields are Jev answering differently. Rerun part with --variants/--rules/--fixes before reading a delta.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100918Z-34fd442f4a978ffa","text":"Socket test harnesses must bind the helper's publish/sendToReader to the HelperServer made in that beforeEach, not the reassigned server variable: an earlier test's run timed out 5 s later and its 'stopped id-1' reached a later test's host (B13's flake, fixed B14).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b51bc99b3aa533a8","sum":"B14: load-proof tests fix the generator clock (setGeneratorClock(() => 0)); find exposed ones by jumping the wall clock 1 s per read. Names are a fill kind (NAME_TERM), withheld only when namesCut; counting names in prose blanked Full name.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T100918Z-d51f417a758957f9","text":"Tests whose answers must not depend on CPU load fix the generator's budget clock with setGeneratorClock(() => 0) (candidates.ts); find exposed tests by making the wall clock jump 1 s per read and rerunning the suite (B14).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100919Z-90979468cad825fe","text":"Names are a fill kind (kinds.ts NAME_TERM): a field that takes a name is withheld only when namesCut (name-like lines or a contact line's names kept out, a partway cap/clock stop, cutAll); counting names that prose mentions blanked Full name on every Messages set (B14).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
